# Business Analysis Case Study: Food Delivery Operations

## 1. Project Overview

This case study examines operational inefficiencies within a food delivery platform and proposes business solutions to improve order management, vendor coordination and customer satisfaction.

**Role:** Business Analyst  
**Industry:** Food Technology / E-commerce  
**Project Type:** Business Process Improvement

## 2. Business Problem

The business is experiencing operational challenges, including:
- Delayed order fulfilment.
- Inconsistent vendor response times.
- Order inaccuracies.
- Poor communication between vendors, riders and customers.
- Limited visibility into order status.

These challenges affect customer satisfaction, operational efficiency and repeat purchases.

## 3. Stakeholder Analysis

| Stakeholder | Interest |
|---|---|
| Customers | Accurate and timely deliveries |
| Vendors | Efficient order management |
| Riders | Clear delivery instructions |
| Operations Team | Order monitoring and issue resolution |
| Management | Revenue growth and customer retention |

## 4. Business Requirements

The proposed solution should:

1. Provide real-time order status updates.
2. Enable vendors to accept or reject orders.
3. Improve coordination between vendors and delivery personnel.
4. Provide an order management dashboard.
5. Enable customer support to track and resolve complaints.

## 5. As-Is Process

1. Customer places an order.
2. Vendor receives the order.
3. Vendor prepares the meal.
4. Rider is assigned.
5. Customer waits for delivery.
6. Customer contacts support if an issue occurs.

**Identified gaps:** Limited order visibility, communication delays and inconsistent escalation procedures.

## 6. Proposed To-Be Process

1. Customer places an order.
2. Vendor receives an instant notification.
3. Vendor accepts the order and confirms preparation time.
4. Operations monitors order progress.
5. Rider receives delivery assignment.
6. Customer receives status notifications.
7. Delivery is completed and feedback is collected.

## 7. Functional Requirements

| Requirement | Priority |
|---|---|
| Order tracking | High |
| Vendor order dashboard | High |
| Rider assignment | High |
| Automated notifications | High |
| Customer complaint management | Medium |
| Performance reporting | Medium |

## 8. Sample User Story

**As a customer**, I want to track my food order in real time so that I know when to expect delivery.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- Customer can view order confirmation.
- Customer can see order preparation status.
- Customer can view rider assignment.
- Customer receives delivery status updates.
- Customer can report an order issue.

## 9. Success Metrics

- Average order fulfilment time.
- Percentage of orders delivered on time.
- Order cancellation rate.
- Customer complaint rate.
- Vendor acceptance time.
- Customer satisfaction score.

## 10. Recommendations

- Introduce structured vendor order management.
- Implement automated notifications.
- Establish order escalation procedures.
- Introduce operational performance dashboards.
- Monitor vendor and rider performance.

## 11. Conclusion

A structured approach to business analysis can help identify operational gaps, improve workflows and translate business challenges into actionable system requirements.
